{
  "name": "AsJsonKeepsJson",
  "comment": "Stage 4 (ruling 8, decision 773): `set %x% = '{\"a\":1}' as json` lands %x% as\n`{item, kind: json}` — json is item's, not text's, because a json value can hold any\nvalue (number, bool, list, dict). Red today — the baseline is dict 5/5; %x!type.name%\nreads \"dict\" (not \"item\"), so the first assert fails before the kind can be checked.",
